<!--Post: 2415--><!--Time: 1103615876-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2415"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 11:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Can someone with a knowledge of Wichita tell me why N. Woodrow &amp;/or 11th St is called &#34;North Of Kechi&#34;? <BR> <BR>Why? &amp; What does this refer to? <BR> <BR> Can someone with a knowledge of Wichita tell me why N. Woodrow &amp;/or 11th St is called &#34;North Of Kechi&#34;? <BR> <BR>Why? &amp; What does this refer to? <BR> <BR>My own investigation brought up an address listed as  &#34;North Of Kechi&#34; with no #s just the name. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2415-->
<!--Post: 2416--><!--Time: 1103615983-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2416"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 11:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oops didn&#39;t mean to double that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2416-->
<!--Post: 2421--><!--Time: 1103637101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2421"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 5:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->North Woodrow and 11th street would be Riverside. It is nowhere near Kechi. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2421-->
<!--Post: 2423--><!--Time: 1103637650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2423"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://img159.exs.cx/img159/7626/postwoodrowand11th4pj.gif" target=_top>http://img159.exs.cx/img159/7626/postwoodrowand11t h4pj.gif</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2423-->
<!--Post: 2437--><!--Time: 1103677920-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 5:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s the deal: <BR> <BR>Someone on another thread asked about railroad maps of Wichita. <BR> <BR>I did a search. <BR> <BR>For some reason the first thing that came up was a Storage Facility and it&#39;s address is simply: <BR> <BR>North of Kechi, Wichita, KS <BR> <BR>The Map puts it on N. Woodrow just at 11th. <BR> <BR>My Question is what does &#34;North of Kechi&#34; refer to &#34;specifically.&#34; <BR> <BR>Not just where but what does Ketchi mean and why is where it is. <BR> <BR>The Map you posted is the same spot the storage facility is at. <BR> <BR>It is right in the middle of the crime scene areas and a short walk to at least one of them. It&#39;s by a park and by rivers and railroad tracks... <BR> <BR>Oh and I forgot to mention the name of the storage facility is: <BR> <BR>B &amp; K Storage.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2437-->
<!--Post: 2438--><!--Time: 1103678093-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 5:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From a Google search of &#34;railroads Wichita&#34; <BR> <BR>Comes up :&#34;Travel &amp; Transportation - Railroads, Wichita, Kansas, KS ...&#34; <BR> <BR>Click on this and the first choice is:  <BR>B &amp; K Storage. <BR> <BR>Map:  <BR> <BR><a href="http://yellowpages.superpages.com/supermaps/mapinit.jsp?SRC=portals&amp;C=Railroads&amp;T=Wichita&amp;S=KS&amp;PP=N&amp;STYPE=S&amp;CID=523168&amp;LID=0107094622&amp;map.x=212&amp;map.y=125&amp;level=8&amp;lat=037704791&amp;lng=-097359156&amp;POI1lat=037704791&amp;POI1lng=-097359156&amp;POI1name=B%2B%26%2BK%2BStorage&amp;streetaddress=North%2BOf%2BKechi&amp;city=Wichita&amp;state=KS&amp;zip=67203" target=_top>http://yellowpages.superpages.com/supermaps/mapini t.jsp?SRC=portals&amp;C=Railroads&amp;T=Wichita&amp;S=KS&amp;PP=N&amp; STYPE=S&amp;CID=523168&amp;LID=0107094622&amp;map.x=212&amp;map.y= 125&amp;level=8&amp;lat=037704791&amp;lng=-097359156&amp;POI1lat=0 37704791&amp;POI1lng=-097359156&amp;POI1name=B&#43;%26&#43;K&#43;Stora ge&amp;streetaddress=North&#43;Of&#43;Kechi&amp;city=Wichita&amp;state =KS&amp;zip=67203</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2438-->
<!--Post: 2440--><!--Time: 1103680157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2440"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 5:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is puzzling for sure. I can tell you with 100% certainty that the area of 11th and Woodrow is in Riverside, miles from Kechi, and it is a residential area. I have lived in the neighborhood the better part of 20 years and I never recall seeing B&amp;K storage in Riverside or anywhere else in Wichita. Now, there are tiny little mom and pop shops scattered through Riverside - The Riverside Perk coffee shop, Curl up and Dye Hair Salon, Abracadabra Printing.....but storage? Seems to be an odd place to put a storage facility. <BR> <BR>Tomorrow I am going to take a drive down 11th street to see what&#39;s over there. What really has me curious now is that I am certain that there is a home on 11th street, just east a few blocks from Sim Park and the Booth Home, and it has in it&#39;s back yard a restored tractor much like the one on the stamp from BTK&#39;s March 17th letter. Also,on the same street, possibly the same house, there is also a birdhouse shaped like the tractor. It doesn&#39;t hang from a tree - it is up on a pole.  <BR> <BR>Here is a map of Kechi, Kansas. It is located way east and north of Riverside.  <BR><a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?Pyt=Tmap&amp;&amp;csz=Kechi%2BKS%2B&amp;Get%A0Map=Get%2BMap" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?Pyt=Tmap&amp;&amp;csz=Kec hi&#43;KS&#43;&amp;Get%A0Map=Get&#43;Map</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2440-->
<!--Post: 2442--><!--Time: 1103681249-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2442"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cougar the address is &#34;North of Kechi Wichita,KS&#34; <BR> <BR>There is no street #... that is odd. <BR> <BR>The fact that it came up in the railroad search is odd too. <BR> <BR>Again... what does &#34;Kechi&#34; refer to? <BR> <BR>This is the phone # &#40;316&#41; 688-1436  <BR> <BR>Since your there would you try calling it and see what you get. It might be the 24 hour attendant type. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2442-->
<!--Post: 2443--><!--Time: 1103681394-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2443"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also it lists this as a description; Dump Trucks, Construction. <BR> <BR>Maybe not a Storage for goods but for construction equipment?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2443-->
<!--Post: 2444--><!--Time: 1103682085-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2444"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kechi, besides being a town in Sedgwick County Kansas, area code 67067, is also an electronic board game invented by a guy named Michael Marcus who goes by the name of Jacques Treatment. It is billed as &#39;Kechi-A Game of Capture.&#39; Link here: <BR><a href="http://www.treatmentlabs.com/kechi.html" target=_top>http://www.treatmentlabs.com/kechi.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2444-->
<!--Post: 2446--><!--Time: 1103682953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2446"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Doubtful that there would be any kind of storage of heavy equipment in that neighborhood. Riverside is an old neighborhood of lovely Victorian homes, bungalows, pretty things. I think the neighborhood association would not permit such a thing. And I think I would remember it if I ever saw it there. I used to live just a few blocks west and one north of that intersection. It&#39;s a quiet, residential area. Off to itself. Much like College Hill. One of the nicer, older areas in Wichita. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2446-->
<!--Post: 2447--><!--Time: 1103683456-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2447"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 6:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just now saw your post about calling the number. I will and I&#39;ll let you know what comes of it.  <BR> <BR>Right off I can tell the number is a land line, east side. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2447-->
<!--Post: 2558--><!--Time: 1103796499-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2558"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 2:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Waiting for your reply Cougar...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2558-->
<!--Post: 2562--><!--Time: 1103807801-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 5:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Q. Sorry for the delay.  <BR> <BR>I drove to 11th and Woodrow yesterday. Crumm Castle Bed and Breakfast sits on the SE corner. Across the street all directions are very nice Riverside homes. No storage facility. No signs for a storage facility. Nothing.  <BR> <BR>Called the number. &#34;Hi. You have reached B&amp;K Enterprises. Please leave a name and number and have a great day.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Perhpas the 11th and Woodrow address is simply a home office? No idea. Or maybe the map and online directory is in error?  <BR> <BR>Hmm... <BR> <BR>Oh....and the home with the tractor in the yard is one block to the north on 12th street.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2562-->
<!--Post: 2567--><!--Time: 1103814254-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2567"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 7:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi!  I live in the Garvey Center here in Wichita.  It sounds like you are talking about that castle looking hotel on Riverside, Cougar, yes?  I gotta tell you, I think about BTK hanging around my area, corresponding with the media and police, right in my own backyard, and it&#39;s exciting to say the least.   <BR> <BR>Q -  <BR>I live right across the street from the Wichita Public Library.  The railroads in Wichita are numerous, as I&#39;m sure you&#39;ve noticed.  I, personally believe this to be a lost cause in finding out the identity of our suspect.  I think it had major influences in his past, and in his upbringing, but not so much anymore to where he will be caught &#34;hanging out on the tracks&#34; so to say.  But, I do see the validity in looking into storage facilities around railways, and I do know of one on the corner of Central and Zoo Blvd.  I believe that&#39;s the correct intersection.  It just looks eerie, and like the kind of place BTK would store things.  If you want me to check for sure on the intersection, I will.  Nice meeting you two!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2567-->
<!--Post: 2570--><!--Time: 1103815941-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2570"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 7:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nice to meet you, Catcher. I remember when your apartment building was the downtown Holiday Inn - site of the infamous sniper shootings. I had my 30th birthday party up in the penthouse there - 29th &#40; 28th? &#41; floor room.  <BR> <BR>I feel the same as you. Ever since last March Wichita has taken on a gothic feel...exciting and frightening at the same time. I drive to the east side almost daily and take the same route each time - central business dist exit off Kellogg and up Broadway, over to William, right past the library. Often I see Police parked at the drive up drop box. I guess since the library drop all collections must be guarded? I don&#39;t know. The first time I saw the Police there they were accompanying a library clerk as she collected materials from the drop so I guess so. Also, I noticed this week that the north side of the duplex at 843 Pershing &#40; Fox scene &#41; is for rent.  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2570-->
<!--Post: 2602--><!--Time: 1103836666-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2602"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 1:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well the online map may be off but the address is still &#34;North of kechi&#34; with &#34;No&#34; street # <BR> <BR>Perhaps you can call back and find out where it is at?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2602-->
<!--Post: 2810--><!--Time: 1104164570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2810"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR>I think the business is: <BR>B &amp; K Service <BR>6811 N Woodlawn St <BR>Kechi, KS, 316-688-1436  <BR> <BR>The phone number is the same.  The Kansas Secretary of State has the following for B &amp; K Service: <BR>B &amp; K SERVICES, L.L.C.  <BR>BEN J BAXTER <BR>6811 WOODLAND <BR>WICHITA, KS 67067  <BR> <BR>Resident Agent <BR>BEN BAXTER,6811 N WOODLAWN,KECHI, KS 67067-0000, however the incorporation lapsed in 2003 for lack of an annual report. <BR> <BR>This address would be a rural sedgwick County address on a gravel road about 1 mile east and 3/4 miles north of Kechi. <BR> <BR>If it&#39;s REALLY important, I can take a digital picture for you. <BR> <BR>However, the Kan. Corporation Comm. shows a current business with the same resident agent: <BR>B &amp; K ENTERPRISES, L.L.C.  <BR>BEN J. BAXTER <BR>3100 N WOODLAWN <BR>WICHITA, KS 67204  <BR> <BR>Incorporation was started in 1998 but never completed &#34;INCOMPLETE FILING -- NEVER ACTIVATED&#34; <BR>  <BR>The current Wichita SBC directory does not have a listing for Ben Baxter, and I&#39;m not sure whats at the 3100 N. Woodlawn address.  Again I can look if it&#39;s really important. <BR>  <BR> <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2810-->
<!--Post: 2848--><!--Time: 1104188986-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2848"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 3:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow... impressive! <BR> <BR>I can&#39;t say it is important but it is interesting where Map Quest placed the local of B&amp;K Storage and it came up in a search of Wichita Railroads. <BR> <BR>Actually can you do the same search on: &#34;PJ&#39;s ABCs 123s Child Care&#34; in Wichita? I put the info I found in the &#34;Real PJ&#39;s&#34; thread. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2848-->
<!--Post: 2948--><!--Time: 1104309448-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2948"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 12:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR>UPDATE on B &amp; K Storage <BR> <BR>1&#41; B &amp; K Storage, 3100 N. Woodlawn &#40;Sedgwick County District Courthouse Records&#41;&#40;personal visit 12/27/2004&#41; <BR>I went to 3100 N Woodlawn.  The address does not exist. &#40;sound familiar?&#41;  Although the west side of the 3100 block is designated as a park [North Chisholm Creek Park], but in reality it’s just heavily overgrown countryside.  The entire east side is a vacant lot approximately 100ft deep.  There are no structures, mailboxes, tents, igloo, dugouts, lean-tos, foxholes etc. on either side of Woodlawn in that block. Zip, nada, zero. Also there are no cuts for driveways in the curbs, and nothing showing old patched cuts either.  Type &#34;3100 N Woodlawn St Wichita, KS 67220&#34;into <a href="http://www.mapquest.com" target=_top>www.mapquest.com</a>, and you get a good idea of the layout. <BR> <BR>I researched real property records for the entire block of 3100 N Woodlawn.  There is no record of private or commercial ownership. <BR> <BR>2&#41; B &amp; K Storage, 6811 Woodlawn <BR> <BR>The same real property records show 6811 N Woodlawn as a single-family residence built in 1989, and owned by &#34;BAXTER, BEN &amp; KENDIRLEY&#34; <BR> <BR>Response to request for similar information on “PJS 123 and Abcs” Child Care <BR> <BR>1&#41; The name  <BR> <BR>I accessed the Kansas Secretary of State’s corporate records.  There are no corporations with the name &#34;PJ&#39;s ABCs 123s Child Care&#34;, and no names that are even remotely close.  However, your posting on the “The Real PJ?” thread has a different spelling for the daycare: “PJs 123 ABCs”, so I checked it too.  It’s not a Kansas corporation either. <BR> [NOTE:  In Kansas, commercial childcare businesses do not have to be a corporation.  They are licensed/regulated by the Kansas Department of Health and Environment/SRS.]  <BR> <BR>HOWEVER, there is a method permitting an individual to advertise as though he/she were incorporated.  See #2 following. <BR> <BR>2&#41; Commercial Internet Listings <BR> <BR>	Kansas’s law permits individuals to “Do Business As” &#40;DBA&#41; followed by a name, which they can use in advertising.  Example: “John Doe dba B.T.K” could legally advertise as  “B.T.K.” <BR> <BR>	There are no listings for “PJs 123 ABCs” in the 2004/2005 Feist or SWB directories  &#40;NOTE: Phone book entries close in mid April of each year.&#41; <BR> .   <BR>This site, &#40;<a href="http://thecityofwichita.com/childcare/" target=_top>http://thecityofwichita.com/childcare/</a>,&#41; is an index of childcare providers in the Wichita area.  It lists “Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs&#34; &#40;316&#41; 265-1825, 401 N. Kansas St. Wichita, KS.   <BR> <BR>AOL CityGuide &#40;<a href="http://dir.digitalcity.com/main.adp?_dlc=150%2b&amp;_dis=1&amp;_dirsview=sponsors&amp;_dirskip=0&amp;_dirletter=&amp;_direxpand=2&amp;_dgid=0%2c116408576&amp;_dgskip=0%2c10&amp;_dircid=116408576&amp;_diradid=0&amp;_diraction=detail&amp;_dircity=Wichita&amp;_dirstate=KS&amp;_dirlat=376922&amp;_dirlong=%2d973372&amp;_dirzip=&amp;_dby=&amp;_dircat=835101&amp;_dirnamesearch=&amp;_diraddress=&amp;_dirdma=wichitaks&amp;_dirpid=" target=_top>http://dir.digitalcity.com/main.adp?_dlc=150%2b&amp;_d is=1&amp;_dirsview=sponsors&amp;_dirskip=0&amp;_dirletter=&amp;_di rexpand=2&amp;_dgid=0%2c116408576&amp;_dgskip=0%2c10&amp;_dirc id=116408576&amp;_diradid=0&amp;_diraction=detail&amp;_dircity =Wichita&amp;_dirstate=KS&amp;_dirlat=376922&amp;_dirlong=%2d9 73372&amp;_dirzip=&amp;_dby=&amp;_dircat=835101&amp;_dirnamesearch =&amp;_diraddress=&amp;_dirdma=wichitaks&amp;_dirpid=</a>&#41; has a listing: “ Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs” with the same address and phone. <BR> <BR>Wichita at a Glance, &#40;<a href="http://www.wichitaataglance.com/list_childcare.htm?SL=p" target=_top>http://www.wichitaataglance.com/list_childcare.htm ?SL=p</a>&#41; has a listing for “Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs” same address/phone <BR> <BR>Kansas Directory of Business listings &#40;<a href="http://www.ks-dir.com/index.htm" target=_top>http://www.ks-dir.com/index.htm</a>&#41; has the name as: “PJS 123 and Abcs” same address/phone. <BR>[NOTE: All names are cut/pasted from the referenced sites] <BR>I checked Sedgwick County real property records for 401 N Kansas: <BR>This is a 1264 sq. ft. residence, wood frame, and two stories tall with an unfinished basement.  It was built in 1915, and is currently owned by Kenny and Michelle Mai. <BR> <BR>My assumption &#40;and assumptions are not facts&#41; is that 401 N Kansas is rental property.  I make this assumption because the same records show: <BR>1.	The mailing address for the owners is different.  It’s in a very upscale area in east Wichita where average residential appraisals are in the hundreds of thousands.  By contrast, the 401 Kansas property appraised for tax purposes at $19,600. <BR>2.	There’s no mortgage on the 401 N Kansas property. <BR>3.	The 401 N Kansas property was reappraised this year &#40;routine&#41;.  On June 8, 2004 an appraiser found the property vacant. &#40;Transient occupancy is typical of rental property&#41; <BR>4.	 A check by Wichita Central Inspection was done at 401 N Kansas on June 18, 2004 for code compliance. “06/08/2004 04:21 CURRENTLY UNOCCUPIED 06/16/2004 11:30 QUALITY CONTROL CHECK”                            <BR>5.	The only permit issued for remodeling at 401 N Kansas was in 1990 for a wood deck. &#40;Minimal maintenance is typical of rental property.&#41; <BR>6.	The Mais’ also own a house at 405 N. Kansas that has a mortgage.  It appraised for tax purposes at $51,100, although on 6/9/2004 it was unoccupied.  &#40;Transient occupancy is typical of rental property&#41; <BR>7.	The east Wichita mailing address &#40;for Court documents concerning 401 N Kansas,&#41; is owned by Mr. Mai.  [<a href="http://www.anywho.com" target=_top>www.anywho.com</a> &#40;SWB database&#41; lists the east Wichita address as Mr. Mai’s residence.} <BR> <BR>My further assumptions &#40;and assumptions are not facts&#41; are: <BR> <BR>1.	That Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs is/was a DBA. <BR>2.	It was formed after April 2004 &#40;it’s not in the phone books, but is in many e-business sites&#41; <BR>3.	The phone number  &#40;316&#41; 265-1825 is not a valid number today.  &#40;SWB keeps a number out-of-service for 6 months after cancellation to prevent “wrong number” calls. <BR>4.	Whoever ran it either was techno-savvy or knew someone who was.  &#40;All advertising is internet based&#41; <BR> <BR>FINAL WEIRD THINGY <BR> <BR>The last BTK letter &#40;KAKE Press Release 10/26/2004&#41; was dropped off in a FedEx box at the Omni Center 2nd &amp; Kansas, two blocks  from “PJs 123 &amp; Abcs” at 401 North Market.  I wonder who was renting 401 N Market from the Mais over Halloween 2004? <BR> <BR>Well I’ll tell you for damn sure, I’m not going to knock on the @!#$# door and ask.	 <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2948-->
<!--Post: 2955--><!--Time: 1104336060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2955"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fascinating work, whoisbtk!  That&#39;s some good research.  There are so many unknowns in this case, anything can be dismissed as circumstance.  I admire your tenacity in this lead, maybe it could be something helpful after all!  In the last paragraph of your post, you changed to &#34;PJs 123 &amp; Abcs” at 401 North Market.  Did you mean 401 N. Kansas, as you referred to previously in your research findings?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2955-->
<!--Post: 2957--><!--Time: 1104339209-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2957"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, I meant 401 N Kansas.  It was late.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2957-->
