<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2965"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very very impressive! <BR> <BR>Sorry I mixed up the letters and #s order. <BR> <BR>If I&#39;m not mistaken the 401 N. Kansas address is also very close to at least one and since they are all relatively close... all the crime scenes. <BR> <BR>Hmmmm... <BR> <BR>Anyway to check who had the business licence or DBA as you put it? <BR> <BR>Also: Cougar... did you ever call back that phone # for B&amp;K Storage? <BR> <BR>It&#39;s probably nothing but it bugs me for two reasons: 1. Where it came up in Map Quest and the Railroad search it came up in. <BR> <BR>2. No matter how much tracing you and whoisbtk have done... it stilll seems to not exist... very strange. <BR> <BR>If you get a person on the phone at least ask them where it is. <BR> <BR>Again... whoisbtk... very impressive but why not go knock on the door... just don&#39;t wait until you see a deaths head moth before you run... sorry jk. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
