<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3003"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 4:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not to intrude, but I searched the Better Business Bureau. I found no listing for B &amp; K Storage. BUT I did find a listing for B &amp; K Enterprises; owned by a Mr. Ben Baxter - phone number of &#40;316&#41; 688-1436.  Hmmm...  And get this, it has a type of business classification as &#34;Landscape Architects/Designers&#34;.  It lists the address as being 3100 North Woodland Street <BR>in Wichita.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3003-->
<!--Post: 3005--><!--Time: 1104368742-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3005"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please let me preface this by saying that this in no way, shape, or form is my way of saying Mr. Baxter is a suspect.  This is just follow-up on previous posts...  Now, I did find the following snipet on the Wichita crime blotter: <BR> <BR>&#34;July 10--3:20 p.m. Ben J. Baxter reported not being able to locate his 10 cows at 6811 N. Woodlawn in Kechi. The animals were later found at 900 N. Woodlawn and returned to their owner, Deputy Matthew Belew reported.&#34; <BR> <BR>So, Kechi must be town.  Is that correct?  If so, is it south of Wichita?  And rural; since he has cows? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3005-->
<!--Post: 3008--><!--Time: 1104370510-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3008"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:dammitslicky@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dee, to Wichitans, Kechi is that little berg north and a little east of Wichita, where you go to buy antiques. It&#39;s a rural spot in the road. Population between 1000 - 1500. I do believe that Kirstie Alley is from there. Her dad owns Buck Alley lumber. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3008-->
<!--Post: 3011--><!--Time: 1104370880-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3011"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just to warn everyone, from this point on all posts containing names &#40;aside from victims, police, media, etc&#41; and phone numbers will be deleted. In fact, I&#39;m also going to delete current posts that have them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3011-->
<!--Post: 3016--><!--Time: 1104372458-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3016"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->REPOSTING of December 29, 2004 - 12:37 am with names phone numbers removed. <BR> <BR>Q  <BR>UPDATE on B &amp; K Storage  <BR> <BR>1&#41; B &amp; K Storage, 3100 N. Woodlawn &#40;Sedgwick County District Courthouse Records&#41;&#40;personal visit 12/27/2004&#41;  <BR>I went to 3100 N Woodlawn. The address does not exist. &#40;sound familiar?&#41; Although the west side of the 3100 block is designated as a park [North Chisholm Creek Park], but in reality it’s just heavily overgrown countryside. The entire east side is a vacant lot approximately 100ft deep. There are no structures, mailboxes, tents, igloo, dugouts, lean-tos, foxholes etc. on either side of Woodlawn in that block. Zip, nada, zero. Also there are no cuts for driveways in the curbs, and nothing showing old patched cuts either. Type &#34;3100 N Woodlawn St Wichita, KS 67220&#34;into <a href="http://www.mapquest.com" target=_top>www.mapquest.com</a>, and you get a good idea of the layout.  <BR> <BR>I researched real property records for the entire block of 3100 N Woodlawn. There is no record of private or commercial ownership.  <BR> <BR>2&#41; B &amp; K Storage, 6811 Woodlawn  <BR> <BR>The same real property records show 6811 N Woodlawn as a single-family residence built in 1989, and owned by &#40;CENSORED&#41; <BR> <BR>Response to request for similar information on “PJS 123 and Abcs” Child Care  <BR> <BR>1&#41; The name  <BR> <BR>I accessed the Kansas Secretary of State’s corporate records. There are no corporations with the name &#34;PJ&#39;s ABCs 123s Child Care&#34;, and no names that are even remotely close. However, your posting on the “The Real PJ?” thread has a different spelling for the daycare: “PJs 123 ABCs”, so I checked it too. It’s not a Kansas corporation either.  <BR>[NOTE: In Kansas, commercial childcare businesses do not have to be a corporation. They are licensed/regulated by the Kansas Department of Health and Environment/SRS.]  <BR> <BR>HOWEVER, there is a method permitting an individual to advertise as though he/she were incorporated. See #2 following.  <BR> <BR>2&#41; Commercial Internet Listings  <BR> <BR>Kansas’s law permits individuals to “Do Business As” &#40;DBA&#41; followed by a name, which they can use in advertising. Example: “John Doe dba B.T.K” could legally advertise as “B.T.K.”  <BR> <BR>There are no listings for “PJs 123 ABCs” in the 2004/2005 Feist or SWB directories &#40;NOTE: Phone book entries close in mid April of each year.&#41;  <BR>.  <BR>This site, &#40;<a href="http://thecityofwichita.com/childcare/" target=_top>http://thecityofwichita.com/childcare/</a>,&#41; is an index of childcare providers in the Wichita area. It lists “Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs&#34; &#40;316&#41; &#40;CENSORED&#41;, 401 N. Kansas St. Wichita, KS.  <BR> <BR>AOL CityGuide &#40;<a href="http://dir.digitalcity.com/main.adp?_dlc=150%2b&amp;_d" target=_top>http://dir.digitalcity.com/main.adp?_dlc=150%2b&amp;_d</a> is=1&amp;_dirsview=sponsors&amp;_dirskip=0&amp;_dirletter=&amp;_di rexpand=2&amp;_dgid=0%2c116408576&amp;_dgskip=0%2c10&amp;_dirc id=116408576&amp;_diradid=0&amp;_diraction=detail&amp;_dircity =Wichita&amp;_dirstate=KS&amp;_dirlat=376922&amp;_dirlong=%2d9 73372&amp;_dirzip=&amp;_dby=&amp;_dircat=835101&amp;_dirnamesearch =&amp;_diraddress=&amp;_dirdma=wichitaks&amp;_dirpid=&#41; has a listing: “ Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs” with the same address and phone.  <BR> <BR>Wichita at a Glance, &#40;<a href="http://www.wichitaataglance.com/list_childcare.htm" target=_top>http://www.wichitaataglance.com/list_childcare.htm</a> ?SL=p&#41; has a listing for “Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs” same address/phone  <BR> <BR>Kansas Directory of Business listings &#40;<a href="http://www.ks-dir.com/index.htm" target=_top>http://www.ks-dir.com/index.htm</a>&#41; has the name as: “PJS 123 and Abcs” same address/phone.  <BR>[NOTE: All names are cut/pasted from the referenced sites]  <BR>I checked Sedgwick County real property records for 401 N Kansas:  <BR>This is a 1264 sq. ft. residence, wood frame, and two stories tall with an unfinished basement. It was built in 1915, and is currently owned by &#40;CENSORED&#41;  <BR> <BR>My assumption &#40;and assumptions are not facts&#41; is that 401 N Kansas is rental property. I make this assumption because the same records show:  <BR>1. The mailing address for the owners is different. It’s in a very upscale area in east Wichita where average residential appraisals are in the hundreds of thousands. By contrast, the 401 Kansas property appraised for tax purposes at $19,600.  <BR>2. There’s no mortgage on the 401 N Kansas property.  <BR>3. The 401 N Kansas property was reappraised this year &#40;routine&#41;. On June 8, 2004 an appraiser found the property vacant. &#40;Transient occupancy is typical of rental property&#41;  <BR>4. A check by Wichita Central Inspection was done at 401 N Kansas on June 18, 2004 for code compliance. “06/08/2004 04:21 CURRENTLY UNOCCUPIED 06/16/2004 11:30 QUALITY CONTROL CHECK”  <BR>5. The only permit issued for remodeling at 401 N Kansas was in 1990 for a wood deck. &#40;Minimal maintenance is typical of rental property.&#41;  <BR>6. The &#40;CENSORED&#41; also own a house at 405 N. Kansas that has a mortgage. It appraised for tax purposes at $51,100, although on 6/9/2004 it was unoccupied. &#40;Transient occupancy is typical of rental property&#41;  <BR>7. The east Wichita mailing address &#40;for Court documents concerning 401 N Kansas,&#41; is owned by &#40;CENSORED&#41;. [<a href="http://www.anywho.com" target=_top>www.anywho.com</a> &#40;SWB database&#41; lists the east Wichita address as &#40;CENSORED&#41;  residence.}  <BR> <BR>My further assumptions &#40;and assumptions are not facts&#41; are:  <BR> <BR>1. That Pjs 123 &amp; Abcs is/was a DBA.  <BR>2. It was formed after April 2004 &#40;it’s not in the phone books, but is in many e-business sites&#41;  <BR>3. The phone number &#40;CENSORED&#41;  is not a valid number today. &#40;SWB keeps a number out-of-service for 6 months after cancellation to prevent “wrong number” calls.  <BR>4. Whoever ran it either was techno-savvy or knew someone who was. &#40;All advertising is internet based&#41;  <BR> <BR>FINAL WEIRD THINGY  <BR> <BR>The last BTK letter &#40;KAKE Press Release 10/26/2004&#41; was dropped off in a FedEx box at the Omni Center 2nd &amp; Kansas, two blocks from “PJs 123 &amp; Abcs” at 401 North Market. I wonder who was renting 401 N Market from the Owners over Halloween 2004?  <BR> <BR>Well I’ll tell you for damn sure, I’m not going to knock on the @!#$# door and ask. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3016-->
<!--Post: 3017--><!--Time: 1104373158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3017"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 8:22 am:   	 <BR>REPOSTING ALL OFFENDING INFORMATION REMOVED	 <BR>  <BR>Q  <BR>I think the business is:  <BR>B &amp; K Service  <BR>6811 N Woodlawn St  <BR>Kechi, KS, &#40;CENSORED&#41;  <BR> <BR>The phone number is the same. The Kansas Secretary of State has the following for B &amp; K Service:  <BR>B &amp; K SERVICES, L.L.C.  <BR>&#40;CENSORED&#41; <BR>6811 WOODLAND  <BR>WICHITA, KS 67067  <BR> <BR>Resident Agent  <BR>&#40;CENSORED&#41;,6811 N WOODLAWN,KECHI, KS 67067-0000, however the incorporation lapsed in 2003 for lack of an annual report.  <BR> <BR>This address would be a rural Sedgwick County address on a gravel road about 1 mile east and 3/4 miles north of Kechi.  <BR> <BR>If it&#39;s REALLY important, I can take a digital picture for you.  <BR> <BR>However, the Kan. Corporation Comm. shows a current business with the same resident agent:  <BR>B &amp; K ENTERPRISES, L.L.C.  <BR>&#40;CENSORED&#41; <BR>3100 N WOODLAWN  <BR>WICHITA, KS 67204  <BR> <BR>Incorporation was started in 1998 but never completed &#34;INCOMPLETE FILING -- NEVER ACTIVATED&#34;  <BR> <BR>The current Wichita SBC directory does not have a listing for &#40;CENSORED&#41;, and I&#39;m not sure what’s at the 3100 N. Woodlawn address. Again I can look if it&#39;s really important.  <BR> <BR>HERE IS THE WEBSITE FOR THE DELETED INFORMATION.The url for the Kansas Secretary of State is: <a href="http://www.accesskansas.org/corporations/index.html" target=_top>http://www.accesskansas.org/corporations/index.htm l</a>.  It’s a free searchable database <BR> <BR>I have set up an email, <a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> If anyone needs the missing information email me and I’ll send it. <BR> <BR>whoisbtk  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3017-->
<!--Post: 3020--><!--Time: 1104373928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3020"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom: <BR> <BR>How should we handle information such as names and phone numbers. <BR>Example: B &amp; K Storage really sounds sinister until you realize that it is the first letter of the first names of the people who run it. <BR> <BR>This is all public information, how do we discuss this case without it. <BR> <BR>If someone asks what do we know about the person who found the bag in the park, how do we respond? <BR> <BR>Not arguing, this is your yard and your swingset, but it seems if we&#39;re all adults, and if we&#39;re all serious about this, there ought to be some way to pass this information around. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3020-->
<!--Post: 3065--><!--Time: 1104415489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3065"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a thought on the 401 N Kansas address.  Is it possible that the owners do not rent the property out?  I have worked with real estate &#40;from the tax collection side&#41; for years and there is a significant number of people who keep properties of which they have no intention of selling or renting out.  Perhaps this address was an original address for the owners of the property and, after their purchase of the home they live in now, they decided to keep it.  This could be for several reasons.  First, they might have had a parent or child that lived there. Secondly, this may have been the address used as a distance-based business, although no real occupancy was used. There are numerous reasons why people own property that is not used. Also, BTK may not have any real connection to the owners, he may have simply noticed the vacancy and capitalized on it.   <BR> <BR>These are just some observations, for the best way to think outside of the box is to not create those boxes to begin with.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3065-->
<!--Post: 3066--><!--Time: 1104415727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3066"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 6:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To clarify my earlier post.  I am simply stating that if BTK  were linked to the Kansas address, this may be simply his own observation doing so&#40;provided he was linked to the businesses&#41;, not any connection to the owners. <BR> <BR>Sorry my earlier post was worded incorrectly.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3066-->
<!--Post: 3117--><!--Time: 1104468558-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3117"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Two things: <BR> <BR>1. I wonder how Map Quest put the local of B7K Storage where it did right in the general area of the crime scenes when  the business if it does exist isn&#39;t anywhere near it. Also it came up as the first choice in a search for Railroad Wichita when I did it. Odd. &#40;Riverside&#41; <BR> <BR>2. The erie thing is that the numerology chart  top left corner is &#34;123&#34; line one -  &#34;ABC&#34; line two - PJs 123 ABCs is supposed to be at the 401 address but doesn&#39;t exist? The local is again as discussed right near well we aklready covered that but really... <BR> <BR>Creepy. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3117-->
<!--Post: 3118--><!--Time: 1104468596-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3118"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B&amp;K not B7K sorry<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3118-->
